index ee783f9..b753602 100644
--- a/scripts/perf/README.md
+++ b/scripts/perf/README.md
@@ -53,3 +53,7 @@ Six one-operation warmups plus at least 100 ms of measured work per runtime/stag
 A candidate optimization needs evidence from matched outputs and relevant feature/corpus regression tests, plus before/after samples on the same host and allocation counts. Registry caching needs thread-safety and state isolation proof. Removing preflight graph snapshots needs equivalent resource validation and failure ordering; simply skipping validation is not an optimization. This harness makes no Rust, WebAssembly, Swift or WebGPU speed claim in advance.

 The [first local baseline](results/2026-10-18-first-native-js.md) records measured costs, output proof, shared-host load, initial warmup limitations, and one bounded optimization proposal.
+
+## Isolated property-cache attribution
+
+`--allocation-only --stages parse-public,parse-public-fresh-registry,property-repeated,property-unique` collects separately instrumented allocation counts without elapsed timing samples. It does not require an idle host and records concurrent load. Record field-name matrices are prepared outside counters. Array index strings and fixed diagnostic long-key construction remain included equally in both versions. The repeated/unique GraphWriter consumer workloads mix raw lone-surrogate UTF-16 strings, existing intern IDs, long keys, repeated fields and more than 64 distinct property names. Preparation records complete source graph hashes plus both consumer graph hashes, intern counts and GraphWriter's inline size. `compare-property.mjs before.json after.json comparison.json` rejects any changed SVG, dimension, graph ID/order, raw string or consumer graph before reporting allocation/peak-memory deltas. These are allocation attribution workloads, not standalone claims about diagram rendering speed.
